{"repositoryId":1266936269,"availability":"available","full":"ChelseaKR/tods-validate","name":"tods-validate","description":"Beta. Validator for Transit Operational Data Standard feeds: the crew runs, deadheads and vehicle assignments that GTFS does not cover. Checks against TODS v2.1.0 with rule IDs that are never renumbered or reused, reports drift against a baseline, and ships a GitHub Action so an agency gates a bad feed before publishing.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":6,"forks":2,"created":"2026-06-12T04:46:04Z","updated":"2026-10-17T14:54:07Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://chelseakr.github.io/tods-validate/","topics":["auto-fix","browser-playground","cal-itp","cli","data-quality","docker","github-action","gtfs","language-server-protocol","mobilitydata","open-data","pre-commit","public-transit","python","sarif","tods","transit-data","transit-operational-data-standard","validator","vscode"],"demo":"https://chelseakr.github.io/tods-validate/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T16:01:55.583Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T16:01:55.583Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T16:01:55.583Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T16:01:55.583Z","stars":6,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A validator for Transit Operational Data Standard (TODS) feeds, with a CLI and a GitHub Action.","TODS is an open standard for describing scheduled transit operations: crew runs, deadheads, vehicle assignments, and other non-public service that GTFS does not cover. It works as an overlay on an agency's GTFS feed. The standard was originally published by Cal-ITP as the Operational Data Standard (ODS) and is now maintained with MobilityData under its current name. This validator checks feeds against the current spec, TODS v2.1.0.","tods-validate reads a TODS package, checks it against the spec, and reports findings in language a scheduler can act on. Each finding s